invariant: INV-16
file: sha512_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: sha512_hw.c's last two rounds of each sixteen take the constants of
  the two rounds before them, one pair off FIPS 180-4 §4.2.3's, so every
  SHA-384 and SHA-512 digest a session computes on the instructions is
  wrong, and it agrees with no peer and with none of this tree's own
  portable digests. CBMC cannot read an intrinsic, so no proof covers this
  file, and bin/sha2_equiv_test is what holds it to sha512.c's second arm.
  The table itself is sha512_round_constants.h's, which
  sha512_compress_blocks.c reads too, and inv50-sha512-round-constant-off-by-one
  changes a word of it. The file has a body on arm64 alone, so the catch
  is the script, which builds the binary for arm64 and runs it under
  qemu-aarch64, whose max model has the instructions on every host. The
  lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
    round_pair(c, &c->cd, &c->ef, &c->gh, &c->ab, c->w7, first + 7);
--- new
    round_pair(c, &c->cd, &c->ef, &c->gh, &c->ab, c->w7, first + 6);
